      "content": "that's a good start but it feels a bit too polite/sanitized for 1954 alabama. i want them to sound more like people who are actually lived in that environment. they wouldn't just be \"pensive,\" they'd probably be more blunt or even angry about the social shifts. can you rewrite it so the dialogue feels a bit more raw and reflects the actual tension and prejudice people were expressing back then? like, they're worried about how it's going to ruin the town or the way things have always been. make it feel more gritty.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
