      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Understood. I will revise the dialogue to reflect a more gritty and tense attitude.\n\n---\n\nINT. LOCAL DINE - DAY\n\nTwo white business owners, HENRY, wearing a tie and pinstripe suit that whispers of his conservative nature, and DAVID, his younger counterpart who hides his discomfort behind a forced smile, sit across the greasy linoleum at \"SHAW'S DODGERS,\" nursing glasses of whiskey.\n\nHENRY:\n(gruff)\nDavid, you seen this new crowd of people from Montgomery? It's all over the news. No more \"separate but equal\", huh?\n\nDAVID:\n(eyes narrowing, barely masking his disdain)\nHuh. Decency's fast-gone then. Just another cherry on top for those gangbangers, ain't it?\n\nHENRY:\n(eyes narrowing too, temper rising)\nAin't no cherry, David. We own the South, man. We’ve built this damn town solid—on sweat and blood, not this... this charity crap. That old Kennedys' nonsense will come crumbling down if we don't hold our ground. The Collins, that power trip, they want to change our whole system, and why shouldn't they?\n\nDAVID:\n(looking away",
